From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:45:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] strip: leave Copilot and wisp's removed extensions out of the
 app

`gulp vscode-darwin-<arch>` builds the built-in GitHub Copilot Chat
extension from extensions/copilot and then patches its ripgrep shim into
the app. wisp's coordinator replaces Copilot, so drop both steps, and
with them the imports that only they used. Upstream already lists
copilot in excludedExtensions, which keeps it out of the generic
extension packaging.

Add the other built-in extensions wisp removes to that list:

- github-authentication and microsoft-authentication: account sign-in.
- github: publishing to GitHub, permalinks, and git credentials through
  GitHub sign-in.
- tunnel-forwarding: port forwarding through Microsoft dev tunnels.
- debug-auto-launch and debug-server-ready: debugger parts, since wisp
  ships no debuggers.
- prompt-basics: the language ids of Copilot's prompt, instruction,
  agent, and skill files.

editor/product.json empties builtInExtensions, which drops js-debug.
build/tsconfig.json types product.json from its contents, and an empty
array becomes never[], so type the one filter over that list.

The development build still loads every folder in extensions/, because
upstream scans the folder when running from source.

